1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,244
Christmas, nineteen eighty.

2
00:00:02,244 --> 00:00:06,916
A pine forest in Suffolk, England, next to two American air bases.

3
00:00:06,916 --> 00:00:11,306
In the dark, soldiers see a light come down between the trees.

4
00:00:11,306 --> 00:00:14,633
What happened next is still argued about today.

5
00:00:15,099 --> 00:00:19,835
Some of the men who were there say they touched a craft from another world.

6
00:00:19,835 --> 00:00:24,633
Others, who wrote down what they saw within days, tell a much smaller story.

7
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:31,307
One officer put it all in a memo, and it became the most famous UFO document in Britain.

8
00:00:31,307 --> 00:00:37,233
Tonight we open the case file, and we compare it with every telling that came after.

9
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:40,700
There is a tape, recorded as events unfolded.

10
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:43,966
There are written statements from the first days.

11
00:00:43,966 --> 00:00:47,166
And there are stories that grew for forty years.

12
00:00:47,166 --> 00:00:48,633
Which one do we trust?

13
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:54,600
Evidence on one side, alien theory on the other, and a verdict at the end.

14
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:57,500
This is the Rendlesham Forest incident.

15
00:01:01,966 --> 00:01:02,695
Item one.

16
00:01:02,695 --> 00:01:03,668
The setting.

17
00:01:03,668 --> 00:01:07,476
East Anglia, England, December nineteen eighty.

18
00:01:07,476 --> 00:01:16,633
Two NATO air bases, RAF Woodbridge and RAF Bentwaters, sit side by side, both run by the United States Air Force.

19
00:01:17,099 --> 00:01:18,601
This was the Cold War.

20
00:01:18,601 --> 00:01:25,700
Fighter jets, a tense alert culture, and young airmen on night patrol, far from home, over the holidays.

21
00:01:26,166 --> 00:01:32,138
Woodbridge sat right beside Rendlesham Forest, a large managed pine plantation.

22
00:01:32,138 --> 00:01:37,733
The base's east gate opened onto a track that led straight into the trees.

23
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:42,530
And beyond the forest, a few miles east, there was the coast.

24
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:43,524
Remember that.

25
00:01:43,524 --> 00:01:49,700
Out there, a lighthouse on Orford Ness swept its beam across the sky every few seconds.

26
00:01:50,166 --> 00:01:59,034
On the night of the twenty-sixth of December, a little after three in the morning, security patrolmen were on duty at the east gate.

27
00:01:59,034 --> 00:02:03,333
Their names: Jim Penniston, John Burroughs, and Edward Cabansag.

28
00:02:03,799 --> 00:02:09,330
Around that same time, a bright fireball crossed the sky over southern England.

29
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:11,010
Astronomers recorded it.

30
00:02:11,010 --> 00:02:12,900
Keep that in your file too.

31
00:02:13,366 --> 00:02:16,030
The guards saw lights drop into the forest.

32
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:18,755
They thought an aircraft might have crashed.

33
00:02:18,755 --> 00:02:21,233
So they asked permission to go and look.

34
00:02:21,699 --> 00:02:22,363
Item two.

35
00:02:22,363 --> 00:02:23,101
Night one.

36
00:02:23,101 --> 00:02:27,157
Penniston and Burroughs walked into the forest on foot.

37
00:02:27,157 --> 00:02:29,221
Cabansag stayed at the gate.

38
00:02:29,221 --> 00:02:32,466
The woods were cold, quiet, and full of fog.

39
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:36,707
What they described next depends heavily on when you ask.

40
00:02:36,707 --> 00:02:39,952
The men wrote their statements in the first days.

41
00:02:39,952 --> 00:02:42,800
So let us start with what those papers say.

42
00:02:43,266 --> 00:02:51,183
The statements, from the airmen and the officers who followed, are dated around the second of January, nineteen eighty-one.

43
00:02:51,183 --> 00:02:52,599
They describe a light.

44
00:02:52,599 --> 00:02:55,366
They describe chasing it through the trees.

45
00:02:55,833 --> 00:03:01,492
And in those original accounts, as the men came closer, the light seemed to move away.

46
00:03:01,492 --> 00:03:06,756
Eventually, they could see it was a beam, sweeping and flashing from a distance.

47
00:03:06,756 --> 00:03:08,533
The Orford Ness lighthouse.

48
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,100
Read that again.

49
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:16,842
In their own first words, the thing they chased through the trees turned out to be the lighthouse.

50
00:03:16,842 --> 00:03:17,942
No landed craft.

51
00:03:17,942 --> 00:03:19,043
No missing time.

52
00:03:19,043 --> 00:03:19,800
No symbols.

53
00:03:20,266 --> 00:03:24,417
Around four in the morning, the local Suffolk police were alerted.

54
00:03:24,417 --> 00:03:25,612
They looked around.

55
00:03:25,612 --> 00:03:29,699
According to the accounts, all they could see was the lighthouse.

56
00:03:30,166 --> 00:03:34,042
But at first light, men went back and found something on the ground.

57
00:03:34,042 --> 00:03:36,322
Shallow depressions in the forest floor.

58
00:03:36,322 --> 00:03:37,633
They were photographed.

59
00:03:38,099 --> 00:03:41,291
Marks like these can be made by many things.

60
00:03:41,291 --> 00:03:42,451
Animals digging.

61
00:03:42,451 --> 00:03:43,539
Rabbit scrapes.

62
00:03:43,539 --> 00:03:44,337
Tree roots.

63
00:03:44,337 --> 00:03:47,166
Nobody can say for sure what made them.

64
00:03:47,633 --> 00:03:53,369
So the first morning ended with a vague incident, some marks, and a stack of statements.

65
00:03:53,369 --> 00:03:56,433
Then, years later, the story started to change.

66
00:03:56,900 --> 00:04:01,408
Jim Penniston, one of the two who went in, began to say much more.

67
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:07,966
A craft, triangular, the size of a car, with a smooth black surface, and symbols he could touch.

68
00:04:08,433 --> 00:04:15,995
He later described binary code, strings of ones and zeros, that he said was downloaded into his mind.

69
00:04:15,995 --> 00:04:18,166
This is the dramatic version.

70
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:21,466
But here is the problem for the case file.

71
00:04:21,466 --> 00:04:25,783
None of this appears in the statements from nineteen eighty-one.

72
00:04:25,783 --> 00:04:27,604
It was added decades later.

73
00:04:27,604 --> 00:04:30,033
Evidence of a story, not of a craft.

74
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,220
Item three.

75
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:31,876
Night two.

76
00:04:31,876 --> 00:04:35,414
The twenty-seventh into the twenty-eighth of December.

77
00:04:35,414 --> 00:04:40,133
Word reached the deputy base commander, Lieutenant Colonel Charles Halt.

78
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:43,798
Halt led a team into the forest to investigate.

79
00:04:43,798 --> 00:04:49,855
He carried a small handheld tape recorder and narrated what was happening as it happened.

80
00:04:49,855 --> 00:04:52,033
That is rare, and very valuable.

81
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:56,063
On the tape, the men describe a light between the trees.

82
00:04:56,063 --> 00:04:57,272
It seemed to pulse.

83
00:04:57,272 --> 00:05:01,600
At one point, they say, it looked like it was dripping molten metal.

84
00:05:02,066 --> 00:05:05,912
Later the group moved to open fields beyond the trees.

85
00:05:05,912 --> 00:05:07,834
Lights appeared in the sky.

86
00:05:07,834 --> 00:05:11,466
On the tape, the voices become tense, then excited.

87
00:05:11,933 --> 00:05:17,393
They also carried a radiation meter, and took readings near the marks in the ground.

88
00:05:17,393 --> 00:05:21,033
Reported as slightly above background, but not alarming.

89
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:23,454
Here is a detail that matters.

90
00:05:23,454 --> 00:05:27,427
Researcher Ian Ridpath compared the tape with the lighthouse.

91
00:05:27,427 --> 00:05:32,899
The light in the distance flashes at the same rate as the lighthouse, over and over.

92
00:05:33,366 --> 00:05:36,830
Halt believed the lighthouse was to the south-east.

93
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:39,071
In fact, it sits almost due east.

94
00:05:39,071 --> 00:05:44,300
Some critics suggest he confused it with another light, a lightship offshore.

95
00:05:44,766 --> 00:05:45,788
And the stars?

96
00:05:45,788 --> 00:05:51,554
On the tape, Halt describes three bright lights in the sky, moving in odd ways.

97
00:05:51,554 --> 00:05:55,933
Bright stars near the horizon can seem to dance in cold air.

98
00:05:56,399 --> 00:05:59,130
None of that proves these men saw nothing.

99
00:05:59,130 --> 00:06:00,170
They saw lights.

100
00:06:00,170 --> 00:06:01,275
They were honest.

101
00:06:01,275 --> 00:06:06,866
The question is what produced them, and whether anyone could read the sky in the dark.

102
00:06:07,333 --> 00:06:09,256
By dawn, the team went home.

103
00:06:09,256 --> 00:06:12,348
Everyone had been scared, excited, and tired.

104
00:06:12,348 --> 00:06:15,233
And somewhere, a report had to be written.

105
00:06:15,699 --> 00:06:16,490
Item four.

106
00:06:16,490 --> 00:06:17,202
The memo.

107
00:06:17,202 --> 00:06:22,024
In Britain, anything unusual near a base was reported upward.

108
00:06:22,024 --> 00:06:28,033
A British liaison officer, Donald Moreland, urged Halt to put it in writing.

109
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:32,872
Halt wrote it on the thirteenth of January, nineteen eighty-one.

110
00:06:32,872 --> 00:06:35,126
About two weeks after the events.

111
00:06:35,126 --> 00:06:39,566
Short, typed, official, and addressed to the Ministry of Defence.

112
00:06:40,033 --> 00:06:49,833
In it, he describes a strange glowing object in the forest, metallic in appearance, and later lights in the sky that seemed to send down beams.

113
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:53,661
The memo stayed quiet until nineteen eighty-three.

114
00:06:53,661 --> 00:06:59,107
Then American researchers, using the Freedom of Information Act, got it released.

115
00:06:59,107 --> 00:07:02,133
It reached newspapers, and the case exploded.

116
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:05,382
The press nicknamed it Britain's Roswell.

117
00:07:05,382 --> 00:07:07,621
Books and documentaries followed.

118
00:07:07,621 --> 00:07:10,199
Each added a little more to the story.

119
00:07:10,666 --> 00:07:13,532
Halt himself has never really backed away.

120
00:07:13,532 --> 00:07:17,763
He has said for decades that something extraordinary happened.

121
00:07:17,763 --> 00:07:20,424
That sincerity is part of the evidence.

122
00:07:20,424 --> 00:07:22,266
But sincerity is not proof.

123
00:07:22,733 --> 00:07:23,482
Item five.

124
00:07:23,482 --> 00:07:24,455
The suspects.

125
00:07:24,455 --> 00:07:30,296
Over the decades, the case has been picked apart by researchers on both sides.

126
00:07:30,296 --> 00:07:33,066
Let us line up the main explanations.

127
00:07:33,533 --> 00:07:34,377
Suspect one.

128
00:07:34,377 --> 00:07:35,292
The fireball.

129
00:07:35,292 --> 00:07:40,711
A bright meteor, or falling space debris, crossing the sky at the right time.

130
00:07:40,711 --> 00:07:44,933
It explains the lights the guards saw drop toward the trees.

131
00:07:45,399 --> 00:07:46,227
Suspect two.

132
00:07:46,227 --> 00:07:47,262
The lighthouse.

133
00:07:47,262 --> 00:07:53,125
It explains the chase on night one, and the steady flashing on the tape on night two.

134
00:07:53,125 --> 00:07:55,333
Ridpath says the match is close.

135
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:56,832
Suspect three.

136
00:07:56,832 --> 00:07:57,570
The stars.

137
00:07:57,570 --> 00:08:01,554
Cold air makes bright stars twinkle and change colour.

138
00:08:01,554 --> 00:08:05,833
It explains lights in the sky that seem to move and flash.

139
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:09,199
What none of them fully explains is the ground.

140
00:08:09,199 --> 00:08:15,000
The marks are small, and they are not proof of anything, but they are still there in the file.

141
00:08:15,466 --> 00:08:17,778
And then there is the human part.

142
00:08:17,778 --> 00:08:25,766
Tired men, a dark forest, a holiday, an officer under pressure, and a story told again and again until it hardens.

143
00:08:26,233 --> 00:08:26,862
Item six.

144
00:08:26,862 --> 00:08:28,401
The stories that grew.

145
00:08:28,401 --> 00:08:30,360
Here is the crucial pattern.

146
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:33,158
The first written statements are simple.

147
00:08:33,158 --> 00:08:36,866
The later books and interviews are far more dramatic.

148
00:08:37,333 --> 00:08:39,304
Each decade added a layer.

149
00:08:39,304 --> 00:08:40,441
Craft landings.

150
00:08:40,441 --> 00:08:41,426
Alien beings.

151
00:08:41,426 --> 00:08:43,322
Messages from the future.

152
00:08:43,322 --> 00:08:46,733
Some of these appear only in recent accounts.

153
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:55,833
Most of the later claims cannot be checked, because they appear years afterwards, from memory, in interviews, with no paperwork from the time.

154
00:08:56,299 --> 00:08:57,448
Alien visitors?

155
00:08:57,448 --> 00:09:00,895
There is not a single piece of hard evidence.

156
00:09:00,895 --> 00:09:01,661
No debris.

157
00:09:01,661 --> 00:09:03,652
No photographs of a craft.

158
00:09:03,652 --> 00:09:06,333
No physical object anyone can test.

159
00:09:06,799 --> 00:09:14,867
What we have is a real, documented, odd night in the woods, and a gap between what was written and what was told later.

160
00:09:14,867 --> 00:09:16,833
That gap is the real mystery.

161
00:09:17,299 --> 00:09:17,863
Debrief.

162
00:09:17,863 --> 00:09:21,033
Time to score the Rendlesham Forest incident.

163
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:27,255
Real men, real forest, real lights, a real tape and a real memo: evidence.

164
00:09:27,255 --> 00:09:31,455
Fireball, lighthouse and stars fit much of it: likely.

165
00:09:31,455 --> 00:09:32,933
Ground marks: open.

166
00:09:33,399 --> 00:09:41,173
Landed craft, binary code, beings, messages from the future: later additions, not in the first statements.

167
00:09:41,173 --> 00:09:44,033
Alien spacecraft: no physical evidence.

168
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,340
The verdict.

169
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:46,530
Probably misread.

170
00:09:46,530 --> 00:09:52,270
A fireball, a lighthouse, and bright stars, seen by honest, tired men in the dark.

171
00:09:52,270 --> 00:09:57,800
But the ground marks, and the way the story grew, are still worth asking about.

172
00:09:58,266 --> 00:10:03,486
Somewhere out there, a young man looked into a dark wood on Christmas night.

173
00:10:03,486 --> 00:10:05,409
What he saw was real to him.

174
00:10:05,409 --> 00:10:08,500
Understanding why takes patience, not belief.

175
00:10:08,966 --> 00:10:15,239
Next case: a book written in a language nobody can read, full of plants that do not exist.

176
00:10:15,239 --> 00:10:17,399
What is the Voynich manuscript?

177
00:10:17,866 --> 00:10:19,765
What do you think the guards saw?

178
00:10:19,765 --> 00:10:23,333
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next case file.
